    "title": "Riverwoods Police Report: Recent Arrests for Domestic Battery and DUI in Early December - NewsBreak",
    "text": "2 hours ago Between December 3 and December 9, 2025, the Riverwoods Police Department reported several arrests. These included one for domestic battery and three for driving under the influence (DUI). All individuals are presumed innocent until proven guilty in court.\nOn December 8, Adam M. Florzak, 44, of Highland Park, was arrested at the Riverwoods Police Department. He was charged with domestic battery causing bodily harm and domestic battery involving insulting or provoking contact. Florzak was taken to Lake County Jail. His court appearance was scheduled for December 9 in Waukegan.\nThree DUI arrests took place over the weekend of December 6-7. Kevin P. Joyce, 44, of Deerfield, was stopped near Lake Cook Road and Portwine Road. He was charged with DUI, speeding, and driving without insurance. Brianna Grace Cheung, 23, of Long Grove, was arrested near Deerfield Road and Milwaukee Avenue for DUI and traffic violations. Magdalena I. Surowka, 40, of Riverwoods, was stopped near Portwine Road and Orange Brace Road for DUI and disobeying a stop sign.\nAll three DUI suspects were processed and released. Their court dates are set for January 8, 2026, at the Lake County Courthouse in Waukegan. Police remind the public that charges are not evidence of guilt and all defendants have the right to a fair trial.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
